*.swp

# Per-run dispatcher artifacts (run.log, per-task summaries, checkpoints).
# These are produced when dispatcher is invoked from inside the repo's
# own working directory during dev/test; they belong in the target
# project's docs/runs/, not in the dispatcher's source tree.
docs/runs/
worktrees-smoke/
worktrees-dogfood/

# The vendored TypeScript parser (unit D4). A SEPARATELY-VERSIONED ARTIFACT and
# not a blob in this history: operator ruling 2026-08-10. `typescript.js` is
# 9.1 MB of third-party code whose only practical review is a digest, so the
# digest is what this repository carries — `TS_VENDORED_PARSER_SHA256` in
# `role_protocol.py`, which is on FLOOR_GLOBS — and the bytes are fetched at
# install time by `python3 -m claude_dispatcher.ts_parser_vendor` and re-hashed
# on every process that renders a TypeScript signature.
#
# NAMED INDIVIDUALLY, not as `ts_signature_fingerprint/`. The helper `main.cjs`
# lives in the same directory, it IS reviewable source, and it MUST stay
# tracked: it is a parser input, it is on FLOOR_GLOBS, and the whole subtree
# glob exists to protect it. A directory-wide ignore here would quietly untrack
# the one file in there the floor can actually see.
/src/claude_dispatcher/ts_signature_fingerprint/typescript.js
/src/claude_dispatcher/ts_signature_fingerprint/LICENSE.typescript.txt
# Interrupted `os.replace` staging from the fetcher, which cleans up after
# itself; ignored so a crashed run cannot leave a file that reads as source.
/src/claude_dispatcher/ts_signature_fingerprint/.*.incoming-*
